{
  "id": "kinet_rig",
  "name": "KinetRig (Ultra-HFR 144–240 FPS Motion & Video Engine)",
  "description": "Zero-dependency Ultra-HFR kinetic motion graphics & video engine (144–240 FPS) using HTML5, GSAP, Three.js & Studio Server with deterministic offline rendering and inline SVGs",
  "manifest_remote_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Reff33/ContextRig/testing/skills_library/kinet_rig.json",
  "install_command": "npx -y skills@latest add https://github.com/Reff33/KinetRig --agent {{agent_flag}} --copy --yes",
  "ai_instructions": "Follow the official KinetRig workflow (https://github.com/Reff33/KinetRig, full guide in rigtools/kinet_rig/SKILL.md):\n\n1. CORE PRINCIPLES:\n   • Zero Runtime Dependencies: Deliverable (index.html) requires ONLY a browser. No React/Remotion/Manim bloat.\n   • Deterministic Ultra-HFR Timeline: All animations strictly driven by tl.time(). Deterministic 144 FPS up to 240 FPS with zero dropped frames.\n   • Procedural Audio & Wyzowl SFX: Built-in Web Audio API synthesis + curated SFX library (`rigtools/kinet_rig/sfx/sounds.json` / `scripts/fetch-sfx.mjs`).\n   • Strict Vector Quality (Zero Emojis): NEVER use system emojis (🤖, ⚡, 🐙, 🧠, 🕷). ALWAYS use resolution-independent Inline SVG vectors (<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\">) with currentColor or brand glow.\n   • Anti-PowerPoint Motion: No static slide deck fades. Continuous 3D camera travel (push-through, whip pan, yaw 3D) or motivated wipes.\n   • Clean Video Export: body.clean-capture auto-hides all UI and cursor during capture with combined video + audio stream.\n\n2. 6-PHASE AGENT WORKFLOW:\n   • Phase 1 (Brief): Topic, Duration (15-30s opener, 30-60s explainer/data), Aspect Ratio (16:9 vs 9:16).\n   • Phase 2 (Style Brief — Three Candidates, One Pick): DO NOT write code yet. Propose 3 candidates with Concept (Opener, Explainer, Data, E-Commerce, Chat), Style Direction, Palette (3 HEX), and Rationale.\n   • Phase 3 (User Approval): Wait for user confirmation.\n   • Phase 4 (Build from Official Starter): Adapt starter template from rigtools/kinet_rig/assets/ (21 official templates) into self-contained index.html.\n   • Phase 5 (Anti-PowerPoint Rules): Continuous world, max 2 text levels per scene, 1 shot = 1 statement (≤ 5 words).\n   • Phase 6 (Clean Ultra-HFR Export & Studio): Fixed top-right dual-state Export dropdown + Studio bridge (`node rigtools/kinet_rig/scripts/server.mjs`), Space/H/M/R keymap, and all-in-one studio render (`node rigtools/kinet_rig/scripts/render.mjs index.html output.mp4 240`).",
  "claude_command": {
    "name": "kinet-rig",
    "content": "# /kinet-rig <brief> [aspect_ratio] [concept/style]\n\nGenerate zero-dependency Ultra-HFR browser motion graphics using KinetRig (144–240 FPS):\n\n1. **Read Full Spec:** Inspect `rigtools/kinet_rig/SKILL.md` and relevant guides under `rigtools/kinet_rig/references/`.\n2. **Style Brief (Three Candidates, One Pick):** Propose 3 Concept Candidates with 3-color palette and rationale. Wait for user approval.\n3. **Official Starters (21 Templates):** Adapt from `rigtools/kinet_rig/assets/` into self-contained `index.html`.\n4. **Anti-PowerPoint & Zero-Emoji Laws:** Continuous camera traveling, zero static slide fades. NEVER use OS emojis; use inline SVG vectors with neon glow.\n5. **Ultra-HFR & Studio Export:** Run Studio preview (`node rigtools/kinet_rig/scripts/server.mjs`) or all-in-one render (`node rigtools/kinet_rig/scripts/render.mjs <file.html> <output.mp4> [fps] [--audio=track.mp3]`)."
  },
